cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use feynjs in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "feynjs: a JavaScript engine for Feynman diagrams"
version: 0.10.2
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  feynjs is a JavaScript engine for Feynman diagrams. A diagram is written as text, in the syntax of
  TikZ-Feynman or MadGraph, and feynjs places every vertex itself, following the conventions of
  published diagrams, and draws it: as SVG in a web page, a Markdown site or an Obsidian note, or as
  TikZ-Feynman code for a LaTeX document. A diagram lays out identically on every platform.
